$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Procedure for the Synthesis of the Carboxamides 1a−i, 1bA−bC, 1dA, 1eA,
and 1fA. The corresponding carboxylic acid (1.5 mmol) was dissolved in
SOCl2 (4 mmol) and stirred for 24 h at rt under a nitrogen atmosphere.
After this period, the reaction mixture was concentrated in vacuum and
diluted with anhydrous DCM (3 mL) under a nitrogen atmosphere. Then the
corresponding acid chloride in DCM was added to a separate RB flask
containing amine (1 mmol) and Et3N (1.1 mmol) in anhydrous DCM (2 mL)
under a nitrogen atmosphere. The reaction mixture was stirred at rt for
10 min, and then the reaction mixture was refluxed for 12 h under a
nitrogen atmosphere. After this period, the reaction mixture was diluted
with DCM (5 mL) and washed with water followed by saturated aqueous
NaHCO3 solution. The combined organic layers were dried over anhydrous
Na2SO4 and concentrated in vacuum, and purification of the resulting
reaction mixture by column chromatography (EtOAc/ hexanes = 30:70). The
corresponding cyclic ether carboxamides 1a−i, 1bA−bC, 1dA, 1eA, and 1fA.
N-(Quinolin-8-yl)tetrahydrofuran-2-carboxamide (1a). Following the
general procedure, 1a was obtained after purification by column
chromatography on silica gel (EtOAc:hexanes = 30:70). HPLC analysis
performed using OD-H (0.46 cm IDR 25 cm length) as a chiral column.
Eluents, flow rate, detection are listed here. Chiral HPLC: OD-H
(isocratic, hexane/isopropanol 90:10:, 1.0 mL/min, PDA at 323.5 nm) Brown
color solid; yield: 95% (230 mg). Mp 85−87 °C; IR (KBr): 3441, 1653,
1554, 1260, 750 cm-1; 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 10.94 (br s, 1H), 8.88
(dd, 1H, J 1 = 4.2 Hz, J 2 = 1.7 Hz), 8.82 (dd, 1H, J 1 = 6.2 Hz, J 2 =
2.8 Hz), 8.17 (dd, 1H, J 1 = 8.3 Hz, J 2 = 1.7 Hz), 7.58− 7.53 (m, 2H),
7.47 (dd, 1H, J 1 = 8.3 Hz, J 2 = 4.2 Hz), 4.64 (dd, 1H, J 1 = 8.4 Hz, J
2 = 5.6 Hz), 4.28−4.23 (m, 1H), 4.08 (dd, 1H, J 1 = 15.2 Hz, J 2 = 7.0
Hz), 2.48−2.39 (m, 1H), 2.32−2.25 (m, 1H), 2.04−1.98 (m, 2H); 13C NMR
(100 MHz, CDCl3): δ 172.1, 148.6, 138.9, 136.2, 133.9, 128.0, 127.2,
121.9, 121.6, 116.5, 79.2, 69.8, 30.5, 25.6; HRMS (ESI): m/z [M + H]+
calcd for C14H15N2O2: 243.1134; found 243.1154.
