$DATUM Synthesis of 6e: compound 6d (80.0 mg, 0.21 mmol) was dissolved in dry
DCM (10 mL) and the flask was cooled to 0°C in an ice bath. EDC (80.2 mg,
0.42 mmol, 2 equiv) and 2-aminothioanisole (40 μL, 0.32 mmol, 1.5 equiv)
were added in a single portion and the reaction mixture was warmed to
room temperature and stirred for an additional 2 h. After filtering the
reaction mixture through a pad of celite, it was washed with saturated
aqueous NaHCO3 (10 mL) and 1 M HCl (20 mL). The combined extracts were
washed with brine (20 mL), dried over Na2SO4 and concentrated in vacuo.
The resulting yellow solid was purified by preparative HPLC. 6e (99 mg,
0.20 mmol, 95%) as a yellow solid. Compound 6e, White power. Positive
ESIMS [M + Na]+ m/z 518; 1H NMR (600 MHz, CDCl3) δ H: 9.79 (1H, s, NH),
8.40 (1H, d, J = 8.0 Hz, H-3''), 7.44 (1H, d, J = 7.8 Hz, H-6''), 7.28
(1H, t, J = 8.0 Hz, H-5''), 7.13 (1H, t, J = 8.0 Hz, H-4''), 4.66 (1H, s,
H-18a), 4.65 (1H, s, H-18b), 4.31 (1H, d, J = 9.6 Hz, H-11), 3.75 (1H,
dd, J = 17.4 and 8.3 Hz, H-8'), 4.47 (1H, d, J = 7.9 Hz, H-14), 2.53 (1H,
dd, J = 11.8, 8.2 Hz, H-7a'), 2.30 (3H, s, SMe), 2.27-2.19 (2H,
overlapped, H-7b' and H-3a), 2.08-2.05 (2H, overlapped, H-3b and H-1a),
1.78 (2H, overlapped, H-12a and H-12b), 1.62-1.45 (5H, m, overlapped,
H-1b, H-2b, H-6a, H-6b, and H-7a), 1.39 (1H, m, H-7b), 1.33-1.21 (3H, m,
overlapped, H-2b, H-8, and H-10), 1.26 (3H, s, H-16), 1.03 (3H, s, H-19),
1.02 (3H, s, H-20), 0.79 (3H, d, J = 6.7 Hz, H-17). 13C NMR (151 MHz,
Pyr) δ H: 175.3 (s, C-9'), 172.7 (s, C-15), 160.4 (s, C-4), 138.7 (s,
C-1''), 131.2 (d, C-6''), 130.3 (s, C-2''), 127.9 (d, C-5''), 125.9 (d,
C-4''), 124.3 (d, C-3''), 103.9 (t, C-18), 85.2 (d, C-11), 49.1 (d,
C-10), 46.1 (d, C-14), 43.6 (s, C-9), 40.9 (s, C-5), 40.2 (d, C-8'), 37.7
(t, C-6), 37.4 (d, C-8), 37.2 (t, C-12), 35.4 (t, C-7'), 34.3 (s, C-13),
33.7 (t, C-3), 28.8 (t, C-2), 28.4 (s, C-7), 26.7(q, C-16), 24.4 (t,
C-1), 21.1 (q, C-17), 17.8 (SMe), 17.2 (q, C-19), 14.4 (q, C-20).
